# CITATION.cff — citation metadata for bce, the blueprint conformance engine.
#
# Software citation metadata only. A preferred paper citation is added only after a real
# manuscript and archival identifier exist; placeholders are never published as metadata.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bce, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "bce — the blueprint conformance engine"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/blueprint-conformance/bce"
abstract: >-
  bce is a development-stage architecture-conformance gate: author
  a blueprint (the durable architectural contract for a repository) and measure
  the code against it — a deterministic conformance score, a fail-closed merge
  gate, and optional hash-chained integrity records that can be checked offline.
authors:
  - name: "Blueprint Conformance contributors"
keywords:
  - architecture conformance
  - engineering blueprint
  - fail-closed gate
  - evidence
  - typescript
